.TH "CSSTRANSFORMVALUE.IS2D" "3JS" "September 10, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSTransformValue.is2D \- CSSTransformValue: is2D property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]is2D\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R] interface returns whether the transform is
2D or 3D.
.PP
\f[CR]is2D\f[R] is \f[CR]true\f[R] only if every
\f[CR]CSSTransformComponent\f[R] in the \f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R] is
itself 2D (see \f[CR]CSSTransformComponent.is2D\f[R]), otherwise it is
\f[CR]false\f[R].
.SH VALUE
A boolean.
\f[CR]true\f[R] if every object in the value is 2D, otherwise
\f[CR]false\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Comparing 2D and 3D transforms
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] transform2D = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTransformValue([
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTranslate(CSS.px(10), CSS.px(20)),
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSScale(2, 3),
]);

console.log(transform2D.is2D); \f[I]// true\f[R]

\f[B]const\f[R] transform3D = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTransformValue([
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTranslate(CSS.px(10), CSS.px(20), CSS.px(30)),
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSScale(2, 3),
]);

console.log(transform3D.is2D); \f[I]// false\f[R]
.EE
